  "storyboard": {
    "home": "A conversation about free time at home. Ana states that she likes to watch TV; Luis states that he likes to listen to music. Those utterances establish preferences. Recognition options illustrate activities, not whether a photographed person likes them.",
    "create": "Friends share creative interests in order: dance, draw, paint. Drawing is clearly pencil on paper; painting clearly uses a brush and paint. The correct image depicts the named activity only; the heard or written speaker supplies I like to.",
    "outside": "The same conversation turns to outdoor interests: ride a bike, take photos, play football. Use clearly safe cycling, an obvious camera/photography action, and association football with a visible football. Teach bike and photos as part of their full phrases.",
    "share": "Sofía asks Ana about football; Ana says no. Luis asks Ana about photos; she says yes. These are coherent different preferences. Invitations follow in 7.7, not in this lesson."
  },
